%N A155070 Primes with nonprime largest digit.
%C A155070 Nonprime digit = 0, 1, 4, 6, 8 and 9.
%C A155070 Zero cannot be the largest digit of any prime number. - _Harvey P. Dale_, Jul 14 2014
%H A155070 Michael S. Branicky, <a href="/A155070/b155070.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%e A155070 11(1=1=nonprime), 19(1<9=nonprime), 29(2<9=nonprime), 41(nonprime=4>1), etc.
%t A155070 Select[Prime[Range[200]],!PrimeQ[Max[IntegerDigits[#]]]&] (* _Harvey P. Dale_, Jul 14 2014 *)
%o A155070 (Python)
%o A155070 from sympy import isprime
%o A155070 def ok(n): return isprime(n) and max(d for d in str(n)) in "014689"
%o A155070 print([k for k in range(600) if ok(k)]) # _Michael S. Branicky_, Oct 04 2026
